# Dependencies are never committed. `lib/` *is* committed, and that is the reason
# `dsh plugin add github:audsiui/-audsiui-dsh-minimax-coding-plan` installs plain
# JavaScript with no build step: there is no `prepare`, so pnpm treats the
# repository as already prepared and links the committed output directly. Edit
# anything under src/, run `npm run build`, and commit `lib/` in the same commit;
# `npm run verify:artifacts` fails when the two have drifted apart. See the
# `//scripts` note in package.json.
node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Dependencies are installed with pnpm by the harness; an npm lockfile would be
# dead weight here and npm's own default .gitignore excludes it from libraries.
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml

*.log
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*

.typert-workspace/

